@page "/Error"

<PageTitle>Error - FluentCss</PageTitle>

<DocHeader Title="Something went wrong"
           Description="An error occurred while processing your request." />

<h2 class="@DocsStyles.H2">Development mode</h2>

<p class="@DocsStyles.P">
    Swapping to the <span class="@DocsStyles.Strong">Development</span> environment will display more
    detailed information about the error that occurred.
</p>

<p class="@DocsStyles.P">
    The <span class="@DocsStyles.Strong">Development</span> environment should not be enabled for
    deployed applications, because it can display sensitive information from exceptions to end users.
    For local debugging, set the
    <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT</code> environment variable to
    <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">Development</code> and restart the app.
</p>
